  "summary": "Mesrop Mashtots, a monk, scholar and linguist, is traditionally credited with creating the Armenian alphabet in 405. He died at Vagharshapat, the Armenian capital, on 17 February 439 or 440, and was buried at Oshakan, which became a pilgrimage site.",
